The time equation composes consistently as well. The complete station-to-car transformation has the Lorentz form $\begin{aligned}
x''&=\gamma_w(x-wt),&
t''&=\gamma_w(t-wx),\end{aligned}$ where $\gamma_w=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-w^2}}.$ Indeed, $\gamma_w=\gamma_u\gamma_v(1+uv),$ which follows by inserting  and simplifying. Two collinear boosts therefore compose to another collinear boost.

