p.src:
Successive subluminal boosts cannot cross $c$. If $u<c$ and $v<c$, then $1-\frac{w}{c}
=
\frac{\left(1-\frac{u}{c}\right)
      \left(1-\frac{v}{c}\right)}
     {1+\frac{uv}{c^2}}
>0.$ Each additional boost can bring the result closer to $c$, but never beyond it. At the limiting value $u=c$, $w=\frac{c+v}{1+v/c}=c.$ The speed of light is a fixed point of the composition law.

